WEBVTT

title-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.810
Loopback Transformer:

title-2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.510
Towards a Unified View of
Residual Looped Transformers.

memory-3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.580
Linear attention keeps
a memory over tokens:

memory-4
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.200
each token writes to a state
that later tokens read.

memory-5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.980
A residual stream is the same
kind of memory over depth:

memory-6
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.240
each block writes an update
that later blocks read.

knobs-7
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:22.520
In this view,

knobs-8
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.980
every residual rule sets three things:

knobs-9
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:26.240
the input's strength,

knobs-10
00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.180
the total weight of the updates,

knobs-11
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.040
and how that weight is shared.

knobs-12
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.200
When the same blocks repeat,

knobs-13
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.200
plain addition lets the
total grow with every pass.

method-14
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.580
Loopback sets the three separately.

method-15
00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.860
The input keeps weight
one on its own path,

method-16
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:43.490
a decay bounds the total,

method-17
00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.380
and attention shares it
across the stored updates.

live-18
00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.310
Here a standard Transformer and Loopback,

live-19
00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:52.810
both at 3B scale,

live-20
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.460
read the same new text.

live-21
00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.710
Loopback is 23% smaller,

live-22
00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.580
and its loss still ends lower.

scale-23
00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:03.060
From 191M to 3B parameters,

scale-24
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.060
Loopback gets lower loss than the standard

scale-25
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:08.800
Transformer with 40–75% of its parameters.

nine-26
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.530
Against seven other looped designs,

nine-27
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:15.053
it has the lowest loss and the highest

nine-28
00:01:15.053 --> 00:01:17.890
benchmark average at all
three sizes we tested.

math-29
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.460
And at 3B parameters,

math-30
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:24.130
it more than doubles
word-problem accuracy,

math-31
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.150
from 2.6% to 6.4%.

outro-32
00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:30.600
That's Loopback.

outro-33
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:31.580
Fewer parameters,

outro-34
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.480
lower loss.

outro-35
00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.880
The paper and code are
on our project page.
